{"id": 1234, "name": "Nimisila Reservoir Metro Park Campground", "read": "2026-10-15", "pages": [{"url": "https://www.summitmetroparks.org/parks-trails/nimisila-reservoir-metro-park/", "lines": []}, {"url": "https://www.summitmetroparks.org/plan-your-visit/", "lines": [], "via": "Overview"}, {"url": "https://www.summitmetroparks.org/activities/", "lines": [], "via": "Overview"}, {"url": "https://www.summitmetroparks.org/activities/camping/", "lines": [" 18 sites have electricity. Three are ADA accessible. | The campground offers a dump station, free of charge for registered campers. Those wishing to use the station who are not registered campers may do so for a fee of $10. | Peak season: May 1 through October 31 | Off-season: November 1 through December 31 and March 1 through April 30. | Campground closed: January – February | Camp Office Hours are 10 a.m. to 6 p.m", "r tents with combined floor space under 200 square feet, or a camper, RV or truck camper and a tent. There are no showers or drinking water at the campground. | Fees & Cancellation | May through October: Electric sites: $33/week night, $38.50/night on weekends (Friday-Sunday) and summer holidays. Non-electric sites: $26.25/week night, $31.50/night on weekends (Friday-Sunday) and summer holidays. A flat processing fee", " fee applies to each reservation. A 25% senior discount is available Monday through Thursday nights during peak season for people 60 and over. | November through December and March through April: Sites with electricity: $27.50/night. Non-electric sites $22/night. A flat processing fee applies to each reservation. No additional discounts. | Fees & Cancellations: Site changes can be made anytime for on-site campers if "], "via": "Camping"}, {"url": "https://www.summitmetroparks.org/reservations/", "lines": [], "via": "Overview"}]}
